id: internalized
name: Internalized
kind: conditions
maxStacks: 1
# Not a Combat Condition: the Internal Attack entry names none. This is the mark that
# holds "while you are not a member of the Combat Encounter", and the name is this
# system's.
combatCondition: no
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Somebody is inside you. Soak Value and Defense Value down by 2(T) until they come
  back out.
text: >
  Internalized: the Internal Attack Maneuver's mark. "While you are not a member of the
  Combat Encounter, reduce their Soak Value and Defense Value by 2(T)."

---

# --- The name is this system's --------------------------------------------------------
#
# The Internal Attack entry names no Condition. What it states is a pair of penalties and
# the span they hold for - "while you are not a member of the Combat Encounter" - and
# something has to hold that, which is what a mark is for here. So the word "Internalized"
# is not one a player will find in the rulebook.
#
# Not a Combat Condition, for the reason Hyped, Analyzed and Braced are not: nothing calls
# it one. The checklist stays the published eighteen.
#
# --- Whose Tier of Power -----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Reduce their Soak Value and Defense Value by 2(T)", and (T) here is read as the Tier of
# Power of whoever is suffering it - which is how every other inflicted penalty in this
# system reads, because a passive runs on whoever holds it. Guard Down's "reduce your Dodge
# Rolls by 2(T)" is the same shape and the same reading.
#
# The other reading is the attacker's Tier, which the sentence will carry: it is their
# Maneuver. If your table takes it that way the number has to come off the attacker and be
# written onto this mark when it is applied, rather than read here - a different shape, not
# a different line.
[passive]
soakValue -= 2(T);
defenseValue -= 2(T);
